$ Building/compiling llama.cpp

Some notes on building → development/AI/software/inference/llama_cpp.

Get the sources:
code {
→ development/version-control-systems/git/commands/clone[git clone] https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp
cd llama.cpp
code }

Query the GPU's compute capability …
code {
$ nvidia-smi --query-gpu=compute_cap --format=csv,noheader
89
code }

… and remember it for later:
code {
GPU_CC=89
code }

Verify that the compiler is able to compile for the desired compute capability:
code {
$ nvcc --list-gpu-arch
…
compute_75
compute_80
compute_86
compute_87
…
code }

Prepare the compilation:
code {
$ cmake -B build                       \
    -DGGML_CUDA=ON                     \
    -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=$GPU_CC \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
code }

Compile the sources:
code {
$ time cmake --build build --config Release -j $(→ Linux/shell/commands/nproc)
code }

